	"Description": "Every Okta modification event (create/update/delete/assign/grant/...) scored by OKTA_RISK_SCORE(\"mod\") and kept at Low priority and above. High volume by design: an audit stream of configuration and account changes. Opt in separately from the detection alerts.\n\nNo consumers are attached. Next step after install: add a consumer flow to this alert (email, Slack, Teams, webhook, Jira, ...) to route it where your team works. Alert events are also written to the shared _alerts tag (Contents._vendor is Okta), so you can search them without a consumer. Each producer is a scheduled search; disable a producer to turn off one detection without turning off the alert.",
